\subsection{Supplementary batch and numerical-integrity checks}
\label{app:supp-audit}

An analysis-only recomputation from the retained batch sums covers all 408 E1 and 108 R0 paired runs (33,852 stored batches). Primary means, raw means and raw second moments reconstruct exactly; the corresponding 118 fitted-coefficient rows, fourteen $H$ contrasts and twelve R0 policy/allocation contrasts agree numerically with the frozen results. It does not reconstruct unsaved round-level trajectories or validate the stationary law. Raw examples, R1/R2 batches and complete restart states are not part of this independent batch audit.

No first/last-half projected contrast in this audit excludes zero under the original $2\times69$ family adjustment. Batch autocorrelation proxies are retained, not interpreted as certified effective sample sizes. Four of the 68 E1 algorithm-cell raw-versus-balance projected differences have nominal intervals excluding zero; the stored balance estimator remains primary. In R0, direct and primary observables are identical by construction, so their agreement is not a separate estimator validation. R0 first- and last-half endpoint allocation contrasts are respectively $0.003098$ and $0.003129$ for SCAFFOLD, and $0.002053$ and $0.002092$ for FedAvg. These post-hoc subdivisions of the same 64 batches support within-tail consistency; they are not extended-burn or extended-tail runs.

The original fourteen short implementation checks and the affine checks pass. The separate full-horizon $H=1$ audit retains 48 strict $10^{-10}$ failures among 132 checks across all regimes; the R0 subset has 24 among 60, independently reproduced here. The maximum R0 coordinate discrepancy is $4.33\times10^{-10}$, whereas the reported all-regime maximum vector discrepancy is about $7.54\times10^{-10}$; these are different norms. A stable endpoint-increment kernel was separately checked on two long R0 $H=1$ paths and reduced their vector discrepancies to about $10^{-12}$. These post-hoc checks neither replace frozen production outputs nor amount to a full-grid stable-kernel rerun. The numerical-identity and precision flags remain in the registry and companion tables.
